Rejected at Step 0 after reading the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1312.5698).

- G and V pass, but H fails on both tracks.
- Track A: the natural planted-star-forest distribution was solved by NAE/DPLL in 15–122 branches across eight `N=128` instances.
- Track B: Lemma 4’s paper-native construction requires 252 mechanical edge assignments and the same 252 assignments after recognizing the alternating-cycle structure—no compression gap.
- A tagged symbolic prototype passed its local gates, but its difficulty came from benchmark-added tags, slots, and a probe, so it is correctly classified as a convenience analogue and retained only for audit.
- The oracle attempt is preserved, but all calls received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded”; this was not used as rejection evidence.

Deliverables:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.5698/REJECTED.md)
- [rejected_gen_1312_5698.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.5698/rejected_gen_1312_5698.py)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.5698/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.5698/.meta.json)
